    "body": "Superseded by normally merged parent PR #449 (`e1a825bda`) which pins mobile `90cae070`. Git ancestry verifies that pin contains merged notification PR #102 (`0c1ee7f`) and its committed physical-device verification record. Closing this earlier pin avoids reverting the later mobile corrections. Its additional root delivery notes remain reviewable here; the canonical mobile evidence is already included in main.\n\nPin the normally merged mobile notification follow-up (#102, `0c1ee7f`) so a notification opened on a fresh installation reaches sign-in without crashing Expo Router. The root navigator now stays mounted while session/permission guards protect screens. The pin retains current mobile main authentication and API contracts; separate draft onboarding PR #104 is not included.\n\nValidation: exact #102 checks passed before merge; merged source passes all 83 suites / 492 tests and the complete release asset/lint/typecheck/config checks. The notification runtime passed fresh notification, cold request, and warm notification checks on iOS and a physical Samsung SM-S928B / Android 16, with no credential submission or business action. The physical QA app is separately signed to preserve the installed Play app; its unregistered Google OAuth identity is explicitly not an authentication qualification. Detailed evidence and limitations are linked in the updated notification audit.\n\nThis PR changes only the mobile pin and its delivery record. Original web/backend #428 remains deployed and live-verified. Corrected production mobile artifacts are being built from the pinned merge through EAS. Store publication and actual availability remain separate, with Alpha 10 and Apple 19 review preserved. Never promote the old failing Android build 11 or build 12 without this fix.\n",
